-- Tests of the circulars' root (l4/lib/circulars-root.l4): what it is asked, asserted. They sit
-- beside it and not in it (the client, 2026-10-22: "assertions about a file
-- should sit next to it, not be included in it"); the site shows them on
-- its page. `make l4` checks circulars-root through this file, which imports it.

IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `circulars-root`

§ `בדיקות שורש החוזרים`

-- What the site's page of this root lists (tools/roots.py): each
-- instrument it includes, its module and its name.
#EVAL map (GIVEN i YIELD CONCAT i's `module`, " | ", i's `title`) `the circulars' instruments`

-- It includes 13 instruments, each once.
#ASSERT count `the circulars' instruments` EQUALS 13
#ASSERT count (nub (map (GIVEN i YIELD i's `module`) `the circulars' instruments`)) EQUALS 13

-- The circulars' own precedence is this root's: the later circular replaces
-- the earlier. An owner's upper-division teacher in January 2010: circular
-- תשס"ט/3 (14.12.2008) and circular תש"ע/2 both speak to the 2008
-- supplement, and this root rules by the later, תש"ע/2.
`an owner's upper-division teacher in January 2010` MEANS
    `teaching case` WITH
        `the salary month`                IS DATE_FROM_DMY 1 1 2010
        `employer`                        IS `employed by another owning body`
        `in post-primary education`       IS TRUE
        `in the upper division`           IS TRUE
        `represented by the secondary teachers' organisation` IS FALSE
        `in a population whose 5% step was put off` IS FALSE
        `combined salary today`           IS 10400
        `supplement 2001 today`           IS 312
        `combined salary in December 2007` IS 10000
        `supplement 2001 in December 2007` IS 300
        `the kind of school`               IS `another school`
        `the interns the teacher mentors`  IS 0
        `the classes in each grade`        IS 0
        `the roles the teacher holds`      IS 0
        `a further role approved by the district manager` IS FALSE

GIVEN i IS A `pay item`, c IS A `teaching case`
GIVETH A STRING
DECIDE `the circulars' ruling, in words` i c IS
    CONSIDER `the collection's ruling` `the circulars' root` i c
    WHEN JUST r THEN CONCAT TOSTRING (r's `the answer`), " | ", r's `governed by`'s `module`, " | ", r's `by the rule`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN "no circular speaks"

#EVAL `the circulars' ruling, in words` `the 2008 public-sector supplement` `an owner's upper-division teacher in January 2010`
#ASSERT (map (GIVEN x YIELD x's `answer`) (`the circulars' claims on` `the 2008 public-sector supplement` `an owner's upper-division teacher in January 2010`)
    EQUALS LIST 308.5056, 515.2472)
#ASSERT (`the circulars' ruling, in words` `the 2008 public-sector supplement` `an owner's upper-division teacher in January 2010`
    EQUALS CONCAT "515.2472 | ", `circular תש"ע/2`'s `module`, " | ", `a later circular replaces an earlier one`)
